==Indonesian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|id|ms|kami}}, from {{inh|id|poz-mly-pro|*kami}}, from {{inh|id|poz-pro|*kami}}, from {{inh|id|map-pro|*kami}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|id|/ˈkä.mi/}}
* {{audio|id|LL-Q9240 (ind)-Xbypass-kami.wav|Audio}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|id|pronoun}}

# [[we]] (exclusive); I and other(s) but not those I am addressing
#: {{ux|id|'''Kami''' sudah pergi ke pasar.|inline=1|'''We''' have been to the market.}}
#* 1966, {{w|National Pledge (Singapore)|National Pledge of Singapore}}
#*: {{ux|ms|'''Kami''', warganegara [[Singapura]],<br>sebagai rakyat yang bersatu padu,<br>tidak kira apa bangsa, bahasa, atau ugama{{...}}|'''We''', the citizens of Singapore,<br>pledge ourselves as one united people,<br>regardless of race, language or religion{{...}}}}
# [[we]]: the speaker/writer alone. {{qualifier|This use of ''we'' is the [[editorial we]], used by writers and others, including royalty—the [[royal we]]—as a less personal substitute for ''I''. The reflexive case of this sense of ''we'' is ''[[ourself]]''.}}
# [[us]] (exclusive); me and other(s) but not those I am addressing
#: {{uxi|id|Dia memberikan '''kami''' makanan.|He gave '''us''' food.}}
# [[our]] (exclusive); my and of other(s) but not of those I am addressing
#: {{ux|id|Bolehkah kamu taruh buku '''kami''' di [[perpustakaan]]?.|inline=1|. Can you put '''our''' books in the library?}}
# [[ours]] (if used with [[milik]], [[punya|kepunyaan]], etc.)
#: {{ux|id|Hak Milik tanah bangsa Indonesia hanya untuk '''kami''' sekalian.|inline=1|It is only we [Indonesians] who have the right to own this Indonesian land.}}

